## B. Adding an agent host (e.g. OpenClaw)

### 1. Branded icon

Same as MCP clients — `branded-icons.ts`.

### 2. Agent landing seed

**`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/hosts/{slug}.ts`** + register in **`agents/seeds.ts`** (`PUBLIC_AGENT_HOST_LANDING_PAGES`) and re-export from **`agents/index.ts`** when needed (and hub copy in `hub.ts` / shared FAQs when needed). Write `heroDescription`, `hubDescription`, `metaDescription`, workflow, audience, and FAQ in ASD-STE100.

**Agent host maintainability (profiles + archetypes):**

| Layer | Path | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Decision scenarios | `agents/decision-scenarios.ts` | Blog-aligned buyer scenarios; `buildAgentHostPickerFaqDescription(slug)` for cross-host FAQ |
| Host profile | `agents/host-profiles.ts` | `uiArchetype`, `traits`, `featureHighlights` (append per tailored ship) |
| UI archetype | `agents/archetypes/*` | Shared setup steps + feature rows (e.g. `messaging-gateway` for OpenClaw/Hermes) |
| Builder | `agents/buildAgentHostLandingPage.ts` | `{name}AgentSeed` → `PublicAgentHostLandingPageViewModel` |

Messaging-gateway hosts: export `{name}AgentSeed` with `messagingGateway` + `messagingGatewayFaq` (or `faqItems` when custom). FAQ deltas go in `overrides: { faqPatchesByTitle, faqItemsAfterFirst, … }` like MCP `cursor.ts` — merged by `mergeAgentLandingFaqItems` in `buildAgentHostLandingPage`. Optional `overrides.audienceCards` and `overrides.firstFeatureSection` mirror MCP Warp/Cursor. Other hosts stay full VMs until migrated. Reference: `hosts/openclaw.ts`, `hosts/hermes.ts`, `archetypes/messaging-gateway-faq.ts`.

Registering in **`agents/seeds.ts`** also auto-wires the sitewide footer **Autonomous Agent Integrations** column via `listPublicAgentHostSeedsForFooter()` — no footer list edit in `config.ts`.

Add host-specific **`skillInstallOptions`** in **`agents/cli-command-reference.ts`** when install differs from OpenClaw (Hermes CLI, Grok Bot workspace + Plugins, etc.).

**Same PR — agent × channel catalog (required):** add **`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/channels/{slug}.ts`** and wire it in **`agents/channels/index.ts`** (see **§5 Channel SEO**). Without this, `/agents/{slug}` omits the **“{Agent}: Every Supported Channels”** grid (`PublicChannelSiblingGrid` via `listPublicAgentChannelsForHub`).

### 3. Messaging / workflow mocks (agent hosts)

Do **not** let new hosts fall through to OpenClaw Telegram/WhatsApp in **`PublicAgentLandingPage.svelte`**. Either reuse Hermes/OpenClaw channel data or add **`web/src/data/{slug}-messaging-channels.ts`** and branch in the landing page map.

| File | Agent-host mocks |
| --- | --- |
| `safariMock.types.ts` + `SafariMockContent.svelte` | `{slug}-docs-overview` + `*DocsOverviewMock.svelte` |
| `terminalMock.types.ts` + `TerminalCommandMockContent.svelte` | `openquok-skill-install-{slug}` when install is terminal-driven |

Telegram-first hosts (OpenClaw, Hermes): `iphone-15-pro` + `agent-chat-schedule`. Desktop-first hosts (Grok Bot): `desktop` workflow mocks.

Wire onboarding: **`OnboardingAgentConnectStep.svelte`** tab + official docs link; **`OnboardingAgentCliStep.svelte`** docs href; **`account/+page.svelte`** landing + guide shortcut cards.

### 4. Docs

**`web/src/content/docs/agent-setup-guides/{slug}.md`** + **`agent-setup-guides/index.md`** `LinkCard`. Cross-link CLI auth / openquok-core as appropriate. Mention the host in **`hubs/agents.ts`**, **`getting-started-for-cli/index.md`**, **`mcp-setup-guides/index.md`** (agent-hosts sentence), **`other-skills/index.md`**, **`channels/tools/skill-builder/faq.ts`**, and **`faq/index.ts`** when OpenClaw/Hermes are named.

### 5. Channel SEO (required for every agent host)

Ship **`/agents/{slug}/{channelSlug}`** pages and the hub **“Every Supported Channels”** section together with the host landing. **`listPublicAgentChannelsForHub`** in **`agents/channels/index.ts`** returns links only when the slug is in **`PUBLIC_AGENT_CHANNEL_HOST_SLUGS`** with configs in **`channelConfigsByHostSlug`**. MCP clients use a different path (all hub channels without per-host files).

**Skill hosts — add in the same PR as the host landing:**

| Step | File / symbol |
| --- | --- |
| 1. Host config + configs | **`web/src/lib/content/constants/agents/channels/{slug}.ts`** — export `{slug}AgentChannelHost` + `{slug}AgentChannelConfigs` via **`buildAgentChannelConfigsForHost(host, listPublicChannelsForHub())`** (copy **`channels/grok-bot.ts`**). |
| 2. Register slug | Append **`'{slug}'`** to **`PUBLIC_AGENT_CHANNEL_HOST_SLUGS`** in **`agents/channels/index.ts`**. |
| 3. Wire maps | Import configs; add **`'{slug}': {slug}AgentChannelConfigs`** to **`channelConfigsByHostSlug`**; append host to **`AGENT_CHANNEL_HOSTS`**. |
| 4. Re-export (optional) | **`export { … } from './{slug}'`** from **`agents/channels/index.ts`** if other modules need the host config. |

**Smoke:** `/agents/{slug}` shows **`PublicChannelSiblingGrid`** (title like **`{AgentLabel}: Every Supported Channels`**); `/agents/{slug}/facebook` (or any catalog channel) resolves via **`getPublicAgentChannelBySlug`**.

**MCP × channel:** no **`agents/channels/{slug}.ts`** — composed per **web-seo-pseo** / **`mcps/channels/index.ts`**. Bento/CLI depth: **add-social-provider-integration** § Programmatic Agent channel SEO.

**Do not** ship a new **`agents/hosts/{slug}.ts`** without **`agents/channels/{slug}.ts`** + **`PUBLIC_AGENT_CHANNEL_HOST_SLUGS`** unless product explicitly defers all channel pages (rare — document why in the PR).

### 6. Skills / CLI

Update `agent/skills/openquok-core/` (`SKILL.md` metadata JSON for the host when discovery differs) and related docs under `getting-started-for-cli` / `cli-usages` only when the host’s install path changes.

### Grok Bot specifics (`grok-bot`)

- **Not** an MCP client — no `mcps/grok-bot.ts`, no `MCP_CLIENTS`, no `mcp-setup-guides/grok-bot.md`.
- Cloud computer + desktop/iOS chat; skill via **`/workspace/openquok-core/SKILL.md`** and **Settings → Plugins** (or `/` in chat).
- Reference implementation: **`hosts/grok-bot.ts`**, **`grok-bot-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`GROK_BOT_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`**, **`channels/grok-bot.ts`**.

### Meta Muse specifics (`meta-muse`)

- **Not** Muse Code — consumer personal agent (custom connectors, Secure VM). **Do not** reuse `mcps/muse-code.ts` or `mcp-setup-guides/muse-code.md` for this host.
- **Not** an MCP client — no `MCP_CLIENTS` entry. Primary path: custom connector from `https://www.openquok.com/api/v1/openapi.json` + programmatic token in Muse credential prompts; optional `openquok-core` / CLI inside the Secure VM; hosted MCP only when the Muse environment exposes it.
- Reference implementation: **`hosts/meta-muse.ts`**, **`meta-muse-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`META_MUSE_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`**, **`channels/meta-muse.ts`**. Mobile-first mocks (`iphone-15-pro`), not OpenClaw Telegram fallback.
- Cross-link **`/agents/muse-code`** and **`mcp-setup-guides/muse-code.md`** in FAQ and docs so readers do not confuse Meta Muse with Muse Code on dev.meta.ai.

### ThinkRail specifics (`thinkrail`)

- **Not** an MCP client — no `mcps/thinkrail.ts`, no `MCP_CLIENTS`, no `mcp-setup-guides/thinkrail.md`. Do **not** add a separate `/agents/pi` host; ThinkRail is the user-facing IDE and pi runs in-process.
- Desktop/CLI worktree IDE; skill via **`~/.pi/agent/skills/openquok-core/SKILL.md`** or worktree **`.pi/skills/openquok-core/SKILL.md`**.
- Reference implementation: **`hosts/thinkrail.ts`**, **`thinkrail-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`THINKRAIL_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`**, **`channels/thinkrail.ts`**. Desktop-first mocks (same pattern as Grok Bot), not Telegram fallback.

### Dots specifics (`dots`)

- **Not** an MCP client — no `MCP_CLIENTS` entry and no `mcp-setup-guides/dots.md`. **Not** the same surface as **ChatGPT MCP** (`/agents/chatgpt`) — Dots are always-on agents with a cloud computer, plugins, Slack/Teams messaging, and Custom Rules.
- **Not** Grok Bot — Grok uses xAI desktop/iOS teammates; Dots live in ChatGPT, Slack, and Teams on OpenAI-managed cloud computers.
- Skill install: **`DOTS_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`** — CLI on the dot cloud computer + SKILL.md via plugins (see **`hosts/dots.ts`**, **`dots-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`channels/dots.ts`**, **`dots-docs-overview`** / **`openquok-skill-install-dots`** mocks). Desktop workflow mocks (Grok Bot pattern), not OpenClaw Telegram fallback.
- Cross-link **`/agents/chatgpt`** and **`/agents/grok-bot`** in FAQ and docs so readers pick the right host (see blog scenario guidance for Grok Bot vs OpenClaw; position Dots for ChatGPT-native + workplace chat).

### Manus specifics (`manus`)

- **Not** an MCP client — no `mcps/manus.ts`, no `MCP_CLIENTS`, no `mcp-setup-guides/manus.md`.
- **Not** Cue — Cue (`cue.im`) is a separate early-access personal-agent app from the same vendor family. Ship **`/agents/manus`** and **`agent-setup-guides/manus.md`** for Manus only. Do **not** add `/agents/cue` unless product explicitly launches Cue as its own OpenQuok host. Cross-link Manus vs Cue in FAQ and docs so readers do not confuse them (same pattern as Meta Muse vs Muse Code).
- Manus 2.0 path: **Skills** (`SKILL.md`, GitHub import, upload, `/` slash command), optional **Cloud Computer** terminal for `@openquok/auto-cli`, plus Studio/web/mobile — not Telegram-first.
- Skill install: **`MANUS_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`** — GitHub folder URL, curl + upload, CLI on Cloud Computer. Official Skills docs: Manus Help Center article on sharing and using Skills.
- Reference implementation: **`hosts/manus.ts`**, **`manus-messaging-channels.ts`**, **`MANUS_SKILL_INSTALL_OPTIONS`**, **`channels/manus.ts`**, **`manus-docs-overview`** / **`openquok-skill-install-manus`** mocks. Desktop-first workflow mocks (Grok Bot pattern), not OpenClaw Telegram fallback.

